#!/usr/bin/env perl
# ABSTRACT: Omni Control Plane - Kubernetes Cluster Management
# PODNAME: ocp

use strict;
use warnings;
use FindBin;
use lib "$FindBin::Bin/../lib";

our $VERSION = '0.001';

use OCP;

exit OCP->run_cli;

__END__

=head1 NAME

ocp - Omni Control Plane CLI

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    # Project and cluster
    ocp init --hetzner                    # initialize project (keys, config, git)
    ocp apply                             # deploy / reconcile, fix drift
    ocp status                            # cluster status and drift
    ocp destroy                           # tear the cluster down

    # Cluster access
    ocp kubeconfig                        # print kubeconfig
    ocp kubeconfig -e                     # merge into ~/.kube/config
    ocp ssh --node police1                # SSH into a node (admin key)

    # Nodes and providers (OCPNode / OCPNodeProvider CRs)
    ocp node ls
    ocp node add worker-1 --role worker
    ocp node rm worker-1
    ocp provider ls
    ocp provider add --name hetzner-fsn1 --type hetzner --token-file token.txt

    # Versions and components
    ocp version                           # OCP and component versions
    ocp update --dry-run                  # what would be updated
    ocp update                            # update components

    # Controller
    ocp deploy-robocop                    # deploy robocop and its CRDs

=head1 DESCRIPTION

OCP (Omni Control Plane) is a self-contained Kubernetes cluster management
tool. It manages the complete lifecycle of RKE2/K3s clusters across multiple
providers (Hetzner Cloud, SSH-accessible servers, localhost).

B<Note:> The recommended way to use OCP is via Docker:

    docker run --rm -it \
      -v $(pwd):/ocp \
      -v ~/.ssh:/home/ocp/.ssh:ro \
      -e HETZNER_API_TOKEN \
      raudssus/ocp apply

The Docker image includes all dependencies and is the primary supported method.
CPAN installation is provided for users who prefer native Perl installations.

=head1 ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

=over 4

=item HETZNER_API_TOKEN

Hetzner Cloud API token. Alternatively kept encrypted in F<secrets.yaml>.

=item OCP_SSH_KEY

Default SSH private key path.

=item KUBECONFIG

Where C<ocp kubeconfig --export> merges the cluster credentials. Only the
first path is used. Defaults to F<~/.kube/config>.

=back

=head1 EXIT STATUS

0 on success, 1 on error. Errors are reported as a single line; run with
C<--verbose> to get the full Perl error including the source location.

=cut
